# [DOCS-GUARD] F4 (23 Sep 26): pin the line endings of the backlog and the rulings, so no script or
# editor setting can rewrite every line of them at once. A whole-file diff is where a destroyed item
# hides. These files are LF in the repository today; `eol=lf` keeps them that way on every machine.
OUTSTANDING.md          text eol=lf
OUTSTANDING-ARCHIVE.md  text eol=lf
DECISIONS.md            text eol=lf
HANDOFF.md              text eol=lf
# [RULINGS-LF-PIN] (21 Oct 26): the rulings split (D137) and the one-line form (D390) added these — every
# area file, every full-row file and the archive, LF in the repository when pinned; a folder pattern
# covers a new area's file too.
DECISIONS-ARCHIVE.md            text eol=lf
.claude/rules/decisions/**      text eol=lf
.claude/decisions-full/**       text eol=lf
# [MERGE-ONCE-RECORDS] (8 Nov 26): the walk ledger and the file map, which the records' settle step
# (raptor-port/scripts/records-merge.mjs) rewrites from git's own copies — LF in the repository when pinned.
# No merge= line: "keep both sides" would double a row edited in place, and GitHub ignores it anyway.
raptor-port/docs/walk-ledger.md  text eol=lf
raptor-port/docs/file-map.md     text eol=lf
